  <text>
    <body>
      <div>
        <head>In the directories</head>
        <p>The Sir Redmond Barry Hotel is in the directories in <ref target="civic?id=Barry%20Street">Barry Street</ref> from 1867 to 1905, on the west side beside <ref target="civic?id=Agra%20Place">Agra Place</ref>. It is No. 41 from 1895. It is not listed in 1900, when the same number is listed as the <ref target="civic?id=Perseverance%20hotel">Perseverance hotel</ref>; the two names are kept apart here.</p>
        <p>The directories list the proprietors as John Flannery (1867), Robt. Newton (1868 to 1872), Margaret Kiernan (1873), M. A. McCulloch (1874 and 1875), John Bullow (1876 and 1877), C. H. Belot (1878), Mrs Emma M. Belot (1879), George Silberberg (1880), Richard L. Dunn (1885), Richard Gough (1890), Henry Hardwick (1895) and T. Allwright (1905).</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Neighbours</head>
        <p>John Snowden, carpenter, is next door at No. 9 from 1867 to 1885, and Edward Pierce, cabinetmaker, on the other side from 1867 to 1873. In 1873 the neighbour is Jno. Flannery, stonemason. John A. Ewart, tailor, is at No. 43 in 1895.</p>
      </div>
